    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1112">

                <pb facs="1478" n="1468" xml:id="pg1468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/12–1445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>”, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-14T12:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 14, 1945—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5860. For Angell No. 99. Categories of beneficiaries in para 1 urtel 139, Dec
                        12<anchor n="57" xml:id="d1112-f1"/> satisfactory. If necessary you are
                    authorized to proceed as proposed your para 2.</p>
                <p>Cognizant of your difficulties re total to be set aside, so approve $25,000,000.
                    Urge, however, that non-monetary gold be addition to this amount since really
                    restitution item.</p>
                <p>Further reference Deptel 84 for Angell Dec 10,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d1112-f2"/>
                    revised view here that Brit proposal to have Board of Trustees administering
                    reparation for victims of Nazi persecution placed under UNO is inacceptable.</p>
                <p>Subject to above recommendations urtel 147, Dec 12<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d1112-f3"/> approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
